545 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 182 0 R
/E (Pulse Width Modulation \(PWM\) is a fundamental technique used to control the position of servo motors. A servo motor interprets the width of a periodic pulse signal to determine its angular position. A standard servo motor expects a control signal with a fixed frequency \(typically ~50 Hz\) and a variable pulse width \(typically 1 ms to 2 ms within a 20 ms period\). The angular position is directly related to the duty cycle of the PWM signal where short pulses implement smaller angle and long pulse for larger angle while it maintains its centered positon with mid pulses.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
